  federal government, in the public domain. https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egretta_thula1.jpg

ops/shapes.png, ops/zone.png
  Generated by tools/make-op-references.py. Public domain.

../reference/ops/
  ImageMagick outputs for the operation tests, made by tools/make-op-references.py from the images above. Same licenses as
  their inputs.

jpeg/duck-*.jpg, jpeg/egret-*.jpg, jpeg/odd-*.jpg, jpeg/exif-*.jpg
  Made by tools/make-jpeg-references.py from ops/duck.png and ops/egret.png above (libjpeg-turbo's cjpeg, or Pillow for the
  CMYK and EXIF files). Public domain, as their sources.

jpeg/testorig.jpg, jpeg/testimgint.jpg, jpeg/testimgari.jpg, jpeg/depth/testorig12.jpg
  Test images from libjpeg-turbo 3.1.4 (https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/tree/3.1.4/testimages), copyright the
  Independent JPEG Group, under the IJG license; its text is in jpeg/README.ijg, included unaltered as that license asks.
  These files are test data only: Egami contains no IJG code.

../reference/jpeg/
  Decodes of the files above by libjpeg-turbo's djpeg (and jpegtran for the upright orientation references), Pillow's reading of
  the EXIF blocks, and manifest.json, made by tools/make-jpeg-references.py. Same licenses as the files they come from.
  encode/ holds the encoder sources (the duck and egret above, reduced or cropped, as PNG) and cjpeg's encodes of them;
  public domain, as their sources.

jpeg/depth/ (all but testorig12.jpg)
  Made by tools/make-jpeg-depth-references.py from ops/duck.png above, with libjpeg-turbo's cjpeg (arithmetic, 12-bit and
  lossless files) and Thomas Richter's libjpeg (arithmetic lossless, odd precisions and the hierarchical file). Public domain, as
  their source. The tools run in Docker as oracles only; Egami contains none of their code.

../reference/jpeg/depth/
  Decodes of the files above by djpeg, or by Richter's libjpeg for the ones libjpeg-turbo cannot read, and manifest.json, made by
  tools/make-jpeg-depth-references.py. Same licenses as the files they come from.

jpeg/transform/
  Made by tools/make-jpeg-transform-references.py from ops/duck.png above, with libjpeg-turbo's cjpeg and ImageMagick (the CMYK
  file). Public domain, as their source.

../reference/jpeg/transform/
  The files above transformed by libjpeg-turbo's jpegtran, and manifest.json, made by tools/make-jpeg-transform-references.py.
  Public domain, as their source. jpegtran runs in Docker as an oracle only; Egami contains none of its code.

fuzz/exif-seeds/
  Seed EXIF blocks for the exif fuzz target: two taken from jpeg/exif-tags.jpg and jpeg/exif-orientation-6.jpg above, and one
  written by ExifData. Public domain.

fuzz/jpeg/, fuzz/exif/, fuzz/tga/, fuzz/jxl-jpeg/, fuzz/avif/, fuzz/av1/
  Inputs the fuzzers found, mutated from the corpus files above; kept as regression tests. Same licenses as their sources.

gif/*.gif, apng/*.png
  Made by tools/make-anim-references.py (Pillow and ImageMagick) from ops/duck.png and ops/egret.png above, or from generated
  shapes. Public domain, as their sources.

../reference/anim/
  Every frame of the files above as Pillow and ImageMagick composite them, and manifest.json, made by
  tools/make-anim-references.py. Public domain, as the files they come from.

bmp/, tga/, qoi/, pnm/
  Made by tools/make-simple-references.py (Pillow, ImageMagick, Netpbm and qoiconv built from the MIT-licensed qoi.h, or
  written byte by byte by the script) from
  ops/duck.png above, reduced, or from generated shapes and patterns. Public domain, as their sources.

../reference/simple/
  The files above decoded by Pillow, ImageMagick and Netpbm, the pixels the script wrote into its hand-made files, and
  manifest.json, made by tools/make-simple-references.py. Public domain, as the files they come from.

fuzz/detect-seeds/
  Copies of one file of each format from the folders above, as seeds for the detect fuzz target. Same licenses as the files
  they copy.

fuzz/ani-seeds/
  Animated cursors written byte by byte for the ani fuzz target, around ico/cursor.cur, ico/cursor-set.cur and ico/bmp4.ico
  and a few raw-bitmap frames of made-up bytes. Public domain, as the files they hold.

fuzz/avif-seeds/, fuzz/avifbox-seeds/, fuzz/av1-seeds/
  Seeds for the AVIF fuzz targets: copies of small files of avif/ (avif-seeds), the same files with their ftyp box taken out
  (avifbox-seeds), and the AV1 data of their primary items (av1-seeds). Same licenses as the files they come from.

fuzz/jxl-seeds/, fuzz/jxlbox-seeds/, fuzz/jxlentropy-seeds/
  Seeds for the JPEG XL fuzz targets: copies of the small files of jxl/ (jxl-seeds), the boxes of jxl/ files and of Egami's
  recompressions of jpeg/ files with their signature, ftyp and codestream boxes taken out (jxlbox-seeds), and entropy streams,
  MA trees with Modular streams and ICC streams of icc/compact/ profiles written by Egami's encoder (jxlentropy-seeds). Same
  licenses as the files they come from; public domain otherwise.

jpeg/duck-ycck.jpg
  Written by tools/make-float-cmyk-references.py with libjpeg-turbo's TurboJPEG from the samples of jpeg/duck-cmyk.jpg (it
  stores CMYK as YCCK). Public domain, as its source.

pfm/
  rgb-*.pfm and gray-*.pfm written byte by byte by a short script; magick-*.pfm and netpbm-*.pfm written by ImageMagick and
  Netpbm's pamtopfm from numbers in ../reference/pfm/pfm-source.json, by tools/make-float-cmyk-references.py. Public domain.

../reference/pfm/, ../reference/jpeg/*.turbo-cmyk.gz
  The PFM files read by ImageMagick, the inputs given to ImageMagick and Netpbm, and duck-cmyk.jpg and duck-ycck.jpg decoded
  by TurboJPEG to raw CMYK, made by tools/make-float-cmyk-references.py. Public domain, as the files they come from.

icc/compact/
  Compact ICC Profiles by Clinton Ingram (https://github.com/saucecontrol/Compact-ICC-Profiles), CC0 1.0 (public domain
  dedication); copied unchanged.

icc/synthetic/
  ICC profiles written byte by byte by tools/make-icc-references.py, covering the LUT tag types and curve forms the compact
  profiles do not. Public domain.

icc/ncolor/
  n-colour output profiles (seven inks, v4; a duotone, v2) written byte by byte by tools/make-ink-profiles.py for the
  multi-ink work. Public domain.

../reference/icc/
  Little CMS's reading of every profile above and its transforms of fixed inputs, made by tools/make-icc-references.py.
  Public domain, as the profiles.

hdr/
  pattern-pq.png and pattern-hlg.png: ramps from 0 to 4,000 cd/m² of gray and saturated Rec. 2020 colors; duck-pq.png and
  duck-hlg.png: ops/duck.png reduced, with its highlights stretched to about 2,000 cd/m². Written by Egami as 16-bit Rec. 2100
  PQ and HLG PNGs with cICP, mDCV and cLLI, by tools/make-hdr-images. Public domain, as their source.

metadata/synthetic/
  JPEG, PNG and GIF files made from ops/duck.png by tools/make-metadata-references.py with ExifTool 12.80 and ImageMagick
  7.1.1: IPTC, Photoshop resources, XMP in every RDF form, Windows XP tags, UserComment encodings, SubjectArea and an IFD1
  thumbnail, ImageMagick's PNG text chunks, and legacy "Raw profile type" PNG chunks written by the script. All metadata
  values are invented. Public domain, as their source.

../reference/metadata/
  ExifTool's reading of every file above (exiftool -j -a -G1 -struct -n), made by tools/make-metadata-references.py. Public
  domain, as the files.

webp/
  WebP files made by tools/make-webp-references.py with libwebp 1.3.2 (its encoder through tools/webpref/webpref.c, img2webp,
  gif2webp and webpmux) from ops/duck.png, ops/egret.png, ops/shapes.png, ops/zone.png, pngsuite/basn6a08.png and basn4a08.png,
  gif/ and apng/ above, with icc/compact/DisplayP3-v4.icc and the EXIF block of jpeg/exif-tags.jpg. Same licenses as their
  sources. libwebp's own test-data files are not included.

../reference/webp/
  libwebp 1.3.2's decodes of the files above (RGBA, raw YUV planes and composed animation frames), and its reading of their
  headers, made by tools/make-webp-references.py. Same licenses as the files.

tiff/
  TIFF files made by tools/make-tiff-references.py from ops/duck.png and ops/egret.png above: base files written byte by byte
  by the script, variants by libtiff 4.6.0's tiffcp, SGILog and WebP files by tools/tiffref/tiffref.c, metadata added by
  exiftool 12.80 (with icc/compact/DisplayP3-v4.icc). All metadata values are invented. Public domain, as their sources.
  libtiff's own sample images are not included (their licenses vary); --pics fetches them into .cache for local tests.

../reference/tiff/
  libtiff 4.6.0's decodes of the files above (raw samples and RGBA), ImageMagick 7.1.1's RGBA for CMYK, YCbCr and Lab pages,
  exiftool's reading of the metadata files, and manifest.json, made by tools/make-tiff-references.py. Public domain, as the
  files they come from.

geometry/
  coded.png, dmap.png, bordered.png, bordered16.png and the page*.png text pages are generated by
  tools/make-geometry-references.py (the pages turned by ImageMagick); no outside content.

../reference/geometry/
  ImageMagick 7.1.1's outputs and kernel tables for the inputs above and ops/zone.png and ops/duck.png, made by
  tools/make-geometry-references.py. Same licenses as the inputs.

ico/, ../reference/ico/
  ICO and CUR files made by tools/make-ico-references.py from ops/duck.png and ops/egret.png above (hand-written entries, Pillow
  12.3 and ImageMagick 7.1.2), and the decodes of every entry by ImageMagick and Pillow. Public domain, as their sources.

psd/, ../reference/psd/
  PSD and PSB files made by tools/make-psd-references.py from ops/duck.png above (written byte by byte, and by ImageMagick
  7.1.2), and their decodes by ImageMagick, Pillow, exiftool and psd-tools. Public domain, as their source.

fuzz/icoentry-seeds/
  Entry data cut from the ico/ files above. Public domain.

analysis/
  duck.png, egret.png, shapes.png and zone.png are copies of the ops/ pictures; duck-q75, duck-half, duck-bright and egret-q75
  are made from them by ImageMagick; tiny-*, grad16-*, alpha-*, gray8, almost-gray and mosaic are generated by
  tools/make-analysis-references.py. Public domain, as their sources.

../reference/analysis/
  ImageMagick 7.1.1's compare metrics, difference images and identify -verbose statistics, and Python imagehash 4.3.1's phash
  and dhash, for the files above, made by tools/make-analysis-references.py. Same licenses as the inputs.

radiance/, ../reference/radiance/
  Radiance pictures made by tools/make-hdr-references.py (tools/hdrref/hdrcorpus.py, and ImageMagick 7.1 for
  desk-magick.hdr) from a 96 x 64 crop of ScanLines/Desk.exr and from generated ramps; the decodes are stb_image's (public
  domain or MIT) or hdrcorpus.py's, as manifest.json says. Desk.exr is from the openexr-images set, Copyright (c) 2004
  Industrial Light & Magic, BSD 3-clause license (see .cache/openexr-images/LICENSE after running the script).

mpf/, ../reference/mpf/
  apple-gainmap-new.jpg and apple-gainmap-old.jpg are libultrahdr's tests/data/apple_gainmap_*.jpg (libultrahdr 2.0.2),
  CC-BY-4.0. uhdr-*.jpg are Ultra HDR files libultrahdr's ultrahdr_app wrote from a 256 x 192 crop of openexr-images'
  ScanLines/Desk.exr (BSD 3-clause, as radiance/ above). stereo-*.jpg and preview.jpg are Multi-Picture files
  tools/hdrref/hdrcorpus.py assembled from ImageMagick gradients; no outside content. The references are ExifTool's MPF
  listings of each file, made by tools/make-hdr-references.py mpf.

exr/, ../reference/exr/
  OpenEXR files tools/hdrref/hdrcorpus.py wrote with OpenEXR 3.5.2 (its Python bindings, exrmaketiled, exrmultipart and
  RgbaOutputFile) from crops of openexr-images' ScanLines/Desk.exr (BSD 3-clause, as radiance/ above) and generated
  channels. The references are OpenEXR's decodes of each file, made by tools/make-hdr-references.py exr.

gainmap/, ../reference/gainmap/
  apple-gainmap-*.jpg are libultrahdr's tests/data/apple_gainmap_*.jpg (libultrahdr 2.0.2), CC-BY-4.0. uhdr-*.jpg are
  Ultra HDR files libultrahdr's ultrahdr_app wrote from crops of openexr-images' ScanLines/Desk.exr (BSD 3-clause, as
  radiance/ above); adobe-xmp.jpg is uhdr-default.jpg with its ISO 21496-1 metadata swapped for Adobe's hdrgm XMP by
  tools/hdrref/hdrcorpus.py. The references are libultrahdr's metadata and linear half-float decodes at three display
  boosts, made by tools/make-hdr-references.py gainmap.

jxl/, ../reference/jxl/
  JPEG XL files made by tools/make-jxl-references.py (tools/jxlref/jxlcorpus.py) with libjxl 0.12.0's cjxl (BSD 3-clause) and
  Squoosh's CLI 0.7.3 (Apache-2.0), run as tools only, from: ops/duck.png and ops/egret.png above and crops of them (public
  domain); apng/pan-rgb.png and apng/sprite-over-previous.png above (public domain); the jpeg/ files above, recompressed
  losslessly (public domain, and IJG for jpeg-testorig.jxl, as testorig.jpg); and, for camera-*.jxl, raw.pixls.us
  developments from libjxl's testdata (external/raw.pixls at 73695d30), CC0 1.0. jxl/libjxl/ holds files copied unchanged
  from libjxl's testdata (https://github.com/libjxl/testdata at 73695d30, jxl/), Copyright the JPEG XL Project Authors, CC BY
  4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The references are djxl 0.12.0's decodes of each file, and
  manifest.json with each file's source and options, jxlinfo's and ExifTool's readings and jxl-oxide 0.12.6's distance from
  djxl. Same licenses as the files they come from.
  The ISO/IEC 18181-3 conformance suite (https://github.com/libjxl/conformance, BSD 3-clause; its pictures' licenses are in
  its testcases/README.md, one of them CC BY-SA 3.0) and Chromium's JPEG XL web test files stay in .cache/jxl and are never
  committed.

